# The player's API URL is runtime config, not a Vite build-time env var:
# the Docker image is built before infra/cdk's ApiStack URL is known, so it
# can't be baked in at `npm run build` time.
#
#   - Deployed (EKS): infra/cdk's FrontendStack passes ApiStack's apiUrl into
#     the pod as the SA_API_URL env var; docker-entrypoint.d/10-write-config.sh
#     writes it into /usr/share/nginx/html/config.js (window.SA_API_URL) at
#     container start.
#   - Local dev (`npm run dev` / `npm run build`): public/config.js sets
#     window.SA_API_URL = "" by default, so src/api.js falls back to reading
#     frontend/public/sa/ (etl/run_local.py output). To test against a real
#     deployed API instead, edit that line locally (don't commit the change) --
#     value = infra/cdk's ApiStack ApiUrl output, e.g.
#     https://xxxxxxxxxx.execute-api.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/api/v1/text-to-speech
